{"name":"Blackwater Park","hex":"#696268","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blackwater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water, especially in a river or other body of water, that has a naturally dark appearance.\nWater that contains dark organic matter such as loam or tannins. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n  Water that is acidic and low in nutrients.","Water that contains dark organic matter such as loam or tannins. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackwater"},{"term":"park","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of land set aside for environment preservation or recreation.","A tract of ground kept in its natural state, about or adjacent to a residence, such as for the preservation of game, for walking, riding, or the like."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bring (something such as a vehicle) to a halt or store in a specified place.","To defer (a matter) until a later date."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/park"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blackwater Park","blocks":[{"text":"Blackwater Park is the fifth studio album by Swedish progressive metal band Opeth. It was released on 12 March 2001, in Europe and a day later in North America through Music for Nations and Koch Records. The album marks the first collaboration between Porcupine Tree frontman Steven Wilson and the band, as Wilson had been brought in to produce the album. This contributed to a shift in Opeth's musical style. The songs \"The Drapery Falls\" and \"Still Day Beneath the Sun\" were released as singles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/45/Blackwaterpark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackwater_Park","wikidata":"Q18616"},{"title":"Blackwater Park (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Blackwater Park was a progressive rock band from Berlin, Germany, with an English vocalist. They released only one album, Dirt Box, which included a cover of The Beatles' \"For No One\". The album was originally released in 1972 and re-released in 1990. The name of the band comes from the name of the gothic mansion setting of Wilkie Collins' The Woman in White."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackwater_Park_(band)","wikidata":"Q3640818"},{"title":"Park","blocks":[{"text":"A park is an area of natural, semi-natural or planted space set aside for human enjoyment and recreation or for the protection of wildlife or natural habitats. Urban parks are green spaces set aside for recreation inside towns and cities. National parks and country parks are green spaces used for recreation in the countryside. State parks and provincial parks are administered by sub-national government states and agencies. Parks may consist of grassy areas, rocks, soil and trees, but may also contain buildings and other artifacts such as monuments, fountains or playground structures. Many parks have fields for playing sports such as baseball and football, and paved areas for games such as basketball. Many parks have trails for walking, biking and other activities. Some parks are built adjacent to bodies of water or watercourses and may comprise a beach or boat dock area. Urban parks often have benches for sitting and may contain picnic tables and barbecue grills."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Halleyparknovember_b_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Halleyparknovember_b_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park","wikidata":"Q22698"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Antalya%2C_Turkey_March_2022_-_D%C3%BCden_Park_Sign.jpg/500px-Antalya%2C_Turkey_March_2022_-_D%C3%BCden_Park_Sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4